## Pipeline Overview

Inputs (per frame)
- RGB stream from a ROS2 camera topic.
- YOLO person detections to create binary masks and temporal identity links (for trajectories).
- Monocular depth from the latest RGB image.

Spatiotemporal attention
- A lightweight CNN encoder processes short RGB+mask histories.
- Multi-head self-attention aggregates temporal evidence to predict a near-future human occupancy heatmap (e.g., 320x320).
- Decoding with skip connections yields a dense heatmap indicating regions likely to be occupied imminently.

Fusion for control
- We fuse (1) attention heatmap (human occupancy), (2) depth map, and (3) grayscale image into a 96x96x3 observation for the DreamerV3 policy (planning/agent code lives outside this repo; here we focus on the perception/attention path and runtime wiring).

